From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:24:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: make a context's layouts ready where it binds a fbfetch
 shader

zink_descriptor_util_init_fbfetch() adds the framebuffer fetch binding
to a context's push descriptor layout, and its only caller was the
create callback of the screen's live shader cache, so only the context
that created a fragment shader using framebuffer fetch got it. The cache
hands the same shader to any context that asks for it, and every guest
context of the host renderer shares one screen. A second context that
bound the shader through a cache hit kept a push layout without the
binding while the shader read it, and KosmicKrisp's ycbcr lookup then
read the immutable samplers of binding 5 past a layout of five bindings.
The host ended in the pipeline's NIR lowering, in one field report.

zink_bind_fs_state() now calls it for a shader that uses framebuffer
fetch, whichever context created the shader. The call is idempotent per
context. It runs where the context's other state changes do, in the
threaded context's batch execution: a bind is queued for it, while a
create callback runs on the thread that makes the shader, a glthread
worker in a host GL context, and there the call wrote the context's push
layout while a batch could be running on it. The call in the create
callback goes, because nothing reads the layout between the create and
the bind: the layout is read when a draw makes its program and writes
its descriptors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.c b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.c
index 7e9b92b2eae5c656664f91471dc05f6c4d61e378..a07fefafd127a9f5722a31a265a0e797c270417d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_program.c
@@ -2432,6 +2432,12 @@ zink_bind_fs_state(struct pipe_context *pctx,
          ctx->ds3_states |= BITFIELD_BIT(ZINK_DS3_BLEND_A2C);
       }
       if (info->fs.uses_fbfetch_output) {
+         /* The screen's live shader cache hands one shader to every context
+          * that asks for it, so the context that created a framebuffer fetch
+          * shader is not the only one that binds it. Each context makes its
+          * own layouts ready for the shader here, on the thread that draws
+          * with them. */
+         zink_descriptor_util_init_fbfetch(ctx);
          if (info->outputs_read & (BITFIELD_BIT(FRAG_RESULT_DEPTH) | BITFIELD_BIT(FRAG_RESULT_STENCIL)))
             ctx->fbfetch_outputs |= BITFIELD_BIT(PIPE_MAX_COLOR_BUFS);
          ctx->fbfetch_outputs |= info->outputs_read >> FRAG_RESULT_DATA0;
@@ -2843,9 +2849,6 @@ zink_create_gfx_shader_state(struct pipe_context *pctx, const struct pipe_shader
    else
       nir = (struct nir_shader *)shader->ir.nir;
 
-   if (nir->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT && nir->info.fs.uses_fbfetch_output)
-      zink_descriptor_util_init_fbfetch(zink_context(pctx));
-
    struct zink_shader *zs = zink_shader_create(zink_screen(pctx->screen), nir);
    if (zink_debug & ZINK_DEBUG_NOBGC)
       gfx_shader_init_job(zs, screen, 0);
